Hi Dennis,

thanks for your reply. I implemented it this way:

q <- ggplot(data = xx, aes(x = Animal, y = Value))
q <- q + geom_bar(stat = "identity")

q <- q + facet_grid(measurement ~ group, scales = "free_x", space =

        "free")
q <- q + opts(title = "Option Space Free")
print(q)

Close to what i was looking for, but  the Yaxis is not free scaled in this case. The values of the bottom plots are not interpretable this way. Also scales = "free_y" or scales = "free" don't get the job done.

Any other suggestions?

Best wishes,

tine

