Hi:

Something like this, perhaps?

ggplot(data = df, mapping = aes(x = as.factor(window), y= treatment)) +
    geom_pointrange( data = df,  stat = "identity",
                     mapping = aes(ymin= lower, ymax=upper)) +

    labs(x = 'Window', y = 'Treatment') +
    facet_grid(office ~ coalition, scales = 'free_y')

This particular arrangement provides different y-ranges for the
various offices. If you reverse the grid arrangement, then you get one
y-axis per coalition.

HTH,
Dennis

